; Singularity VR mod - settings
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; IF THE GAME WILL NOT REACH ITS MENUS, set this to 0 and relaunch.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; HookUserPointerDraws controls whether the two user-pointer draw calls
; (DrawPrimitiveUP / DrawIndexedPrimitiveUP) are intercepted. UE3 uses them for
; dynamic geometry - particles, decals, sprites - and leaving them alone means
; those draws never get split per eye, so a centred one lands on the seam
; between the two eye halves and disappears.
;
; Hooking them once stopped the game reaching its menus, and that is still
; unexplained: the vtable slots are confirmed correct against d3d9.h, and the
; hooks do nothing at all until F1 is pressed. Since a bad interaction here
; blocks launching entirely, it is switchable here rather than needing a rebuild.
;
; 1 = hooked (default)   0 = left alone

[Render]
HookUserPointerDraws=0

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; There is deliberately no resolution setting.
;
; Forcing the D3D9 backbuffer does NOT raise UE3's render resolution - the
; engine sizes its scene targets from its own configured resolution, so
; overriding the backbuffer only desynchronises the two and switches stereo off.
;
; To change resolution, pass it on the command line, which the engine reads into
; its own system settings:
;
;   Singularity.exe -ResX=3840 -ResY=2160 -windowed
;
; -windowed is needed because fullscreen clamps to real display modes. Note
; 4992x2688 is refused; the cap appears to be around 4096.
